Keep the Word document as a readable publication artifact if you want, but make article.md the easy-to-review source version. Include a requirements file, exact run instructions, and a results template. Commit only results you actually measured. If you publish logs, inspect them first and remove personal or environment-specific data.
23.1 Suggested requirements.txt
requests>=2.31,<3
playwright>=1.40
For strict reproducibility, pin the exact versions you tested after running the lab, rather than treating the broad ranges above as a verified environment. Playwright also requires its browser binary to be installed separately.
23.2 Suggested .gitignore
__pycache__/
.venv/
venv/
.env
*.log
results/raw/
.DS_Store
